    "1/1": "Let's break down the bug scenario and root cause, then generate the required patch.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Bug Scenario Image & Reasoning\n\n**Image Description & Reasoning:**\n- The image shows the `TableHeader` component.\n- For **non-sortable** headers, the `...rest` props are spread on the `<th>` element (correct).\n- For **sortable** headers, the `...rest` props are spread on the **inner `<button>`** instead of the `<th>`.\n- The user wants to set attributes like `id` on the `<th>`, but for sortable headers, these props are not applied to `<th>`, causing accessibility issues (e.g., missing `id` on `<th>`).\n\n**Root Cause:**\n- The `...rest` props are incorrectly spread on the `<button>` for sortable headers, not on the `<th>`. They should be spread on the `<th>` in both cases.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Bug Code Snippet Analysis\n\n**File:** `packages/react/src/components/DataTable/TableHeader.js`\n\n- **Non-sortable:**  \n  ```js\n  <th\n    {...rest}\n    className={headerClassName}\n    ...\n  >\n  ```\n  (Correct)\n\n- **Sortable:**  \n  ```js\n  <th\n    aria-sort={ariaSort}\n    className={headerClassName}\n    colSpan={colSpan}\n    ref={ref}\n    scope={scope}>\n    ...\n    <button\n      ...\n      {...rest}>\n  ```\n  (Bug: `...rest` is on `<button>`, not `<th>`)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Patch Generation\n\n**Goal:**  \n- Move `{...rest}` from the `<button>` to the `<th>` for sortable headers.\n\n---\n\n```javascript\n### packages/react/src/components/DataTable/TableHeader.js\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n  return (\n    <th\n      aria-sort={ariaSort}\n      className={headerClassName}\n      colSpan={colSpan}\n      ref={ref}\n      scope={scope}>\n      <div style={{ display: 'none' }} id={uniqueId}>\n        {sortDescription}\n      </div>\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        aria-describedby={uniqueId}\n        className={className}\n        onClick={onClick}\n        {...rest}>\n        <span className={`${prefix}--table-sort__flex`}>\n          <div className={`${prefix}--table-header-label`}>{children}</div>\n          <Arrow className={`${prefix}--table-sort__icon`} />\n          <Arrows className={`${prefix}--table-sort__icon-unsorted`} />\n        </span>\n      </button>\n    </th>\n  );\n=======\n  return (\n    <th\n      aria-sort={ariaSort}\n      className={headerClassName}\n      colSpan={colSpan}\n      ref={ref}\n      scope={scope}\n      {...rest}>\n      <div style={{ display: 'none' }} id={uniqueId}>\n        {sortDescription}\n      </div>\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        aria-describedby={uniqueId}\n        className={className}\n        onClick={onClick}>\n        <span className={`${prefix}--table-sort__flex`}>\n          <div className={`${prefix}--table-header-label`}>{children}</div>\n          <Arrow className={`${prefix}--table-sort__icon`} />\n          <Arrows className={`${prefix}--table-sort__icon-unsorted`} />\n        </span>\n      </button>\n    </th>\n  );\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \n- The patch moves `{...rest}` from the `<button>` to the `<th>` for sortable headers, ensuring all extra props (like `id`) are applied to the correct element for both sortable and non-sortable headers, fixing the accessibility issue."
